sequence v0
participant Creator
participant Studio tone=system
participant Backend tone=system
participant RSSFeed "RSS feed" tone=system
participant OwnerInbox "Owner's inbox"

section "Claim"
Creator --> Studio: Sign in, no show yet
Studio -.-> Creator: Claim existing, Add via RSS, Start from scratch
Creator --> Studio: Claim existing show
Studio --> Backend: POST claim for show
Backend --> RSSFeed: Fetch feed live
RSSFeed -.-> Backend: itunes owner email
# Messages 7–15 illustrate handshake details, not an agreed product protocol.
Backend --> OwnerInbox: Send 6-digit code
note over Backend: The code expires after 15 minutes
OwnerInbox -.-> Creator: Email with the code
section "Verify"
Creator --> Studio: Enter code
Studio --> Backend: POST verify code
Backend --> Backend: Check code and expiry
alt Code matches
Backend -.-> Studio: Claim confirmed
Studio -.-> Creator: The show is yours
else Wrong or expired code
Backend -.-> Studio: Rejected, attempts left
Studio -.-> Creator: Try again or resend the code
end

play "Claim the show"
  step 1 "Open the studio with no show yet"
  step 2 "Offer the three ways to add a show"
  step 3 "Choose the existing show"
  step 4 "Ask the backend to start a claim"
  step 5 "Read the feed as it is now"
  step 6 "The feed names the owner's email"
  step 7 "Mail a 6-digit code to that address"
  step 8 "The owner reads the code"
  step 9 "Type the code into the studio"
  step 10 "Send it on for checking"
  step 11 "Compare code and expiry"
  step 12 "The code matches"
  step 13 "The show now belongs to the creator"

play "Wrong code"
  step 9 "Type a code that no longer works"
  step 10 "Send it on for checking"
  step 11 "Compare code and expiry"
  step 14 "Reject it and count the attempt"
  step 15 "Offer another try or a new code"
